title: Microsoft Hyper-V VM: RAM
agents: windows
catalog: os/virtual
license: GPLv2
distribution: check_mk
description:
 This check monitors the RAM assigned to a virtual machine running on
 Microsoft Hyper-V and shows the memory demand of the guest. For VMs with
 dynamic memory it also shows the startup, minimum and maximum RAM.

 Levels are configured with the rule "Hyper-V VM RAM". The upper levels are
 a percentage of the configured maximum RAM, the lower levels a percentage
 of the configured minimum RAM. Both have no levels by default.

 The same rule can make the check {WARN} if the demand is higher than the
 assigned RAM. The demand is only shown if the guest reports it.

 The data is collected by the agent plug-in {hyperv_host.ps1}, which can be
 deployed with the agent bakery rule "Hyper-V". The plug-in sends the data
 as piggyback data to a host with the name of the VM.

discovery:
 One service is created on the piggyback host of each VM.
